key insight
The customer base is heavily dominated by one-time buyers, with no observed successful repeat purchases.
Coupon usage did not show a measurable relationship with repeat purchase because both coupon and non-coupon customers had a 0% successful repeat purchase rate.
No acquisition channel generated an observed successful repeat customer, so channel-level retention performance cannot yet be reliably compared.
Only 231 of 1,200 orders were Delivered, indicating that order completion and fulfillment may be an important area for further investigation.

recommendation
Prioritize second-purchase conversion rather than broad retention campaigns.
o not optimize acquisition channels based on retention yet. First collect more repeat-purchase data, then compare customer quality across acquisition channels.
